// The Superverse business protocol (docs/api/resource-grpc.md). Buf STANDARD lint and scripts/check-proto-services.py enforce these
// conventions:
//
// - A service holds at most 10 RPCs of one domain. RPC names are unique across services, and a
//   name starts with Watch exactly when the RPC streams from the server.
// - Each RPC has its own <Rpc>Request and <Rpc>Response. A response that returns a shared DTO
//   wraps it in one field named after the resource.
// - A request names its resource with flat string IDs first, in hierarchy order. Every request
//   except RegisterAccountRequest and LoginRequest carries `CallerContext caller = 100`, which
//   only the Studio BFF sets; no other field is numbered 100 or higher.
// - request_id identifies a deduplicated start or command. The fences are expected_revision (the
//   addressed resource), generation with workspace_request_id (the Sandbox instance) and
//   expected_live_revision (the Project's Live pointer). The BFF fills in no ID and no fence.
// - Integer types follow the Go domain type: uint64 for revisions, generations and fences; int64
//   for Agent sequences, todo list revisions, repository_id and after_event_id; int32
//   where Go holds int32 (page sizes, exit codes, AgentEvent.attempt and the Dex numeric
//   pass-through values); uint32 only for FlowApiDocument.http_status.
// - Times are google.protobuf.Timestamp, except the RFC 3339 strings of the Agent DTOs (the Agent
//   conversation contract).
// - A request of a service the browser reaches through /api/rpc carries JSON in `string *_json`
//   fields, which the server type-checks when it parses them, and reaches no bytes, map, Struct,
//   Value, ListValue or Timestamp field.
// - A closed status set is an enum whose value names are the enum prefix plus the persisted domain
//   value, so Dex keyword3 search values stay unchanged; zero is UNSPECIFIED and means absent.
//   Open sets (failure codes and phases, progress phases, model IDs, reasoning efforts) stay
//   strings.
// - A list request takes page_size (0 means 50, at most 100), page_token and repeated statuses,
//   where a zero or undeclared status is invalid; its response returns the items and
//   next_page_token.
// - Watch<R>Response is `oneof event {snapshot 1; progress 2}` with resume_cursor 3, and the first
//   frame is always a snapshot.
// - A start returns only the ID of the resource it started. A command returns an empty response,
//   or the snapshot the page renders next. No response echoes the caller's other inputs.
// - Surviving fields keep their numbers. Before launch, removed fields are deleted without
//   `reserved`. Fields are declared in ascending number order; a oneof sorts by its lowest member.
// - AppManifestSnapshot, ObjectReference, ConnectorRequirement and ConnectorTriggerBinding are
//   persisted in Dex Attributes as JSON keyed by their field names, so they are frozen.
// - Acronyms are written as words (FlowApi, ConnectorUi); OAuth is the one exception.
//
// The browser reaches AccountService only through /api/auth, the four Flow API services only
// through /dex/... and the other ten services only through /api/rpc/<Method>.

